// Granted by Pixie's Explosive Rounds passive ascension (see ExplosiveRoundsPassiveUpgradeData) -
// while present, WeaponSystem.Equip/ApplyPixieExplosiveWeapon makes every one of her weapon shots
// ELIGIBLE to proc a small explosion (Weapon.ExplosiveSequenceInterval = 1, reusing the Explosive
// Sequence perk pipeline unchanged), and then gates how often that actually happens on ProcChance
// below. As a side effect (HitEffectUtility.ApplyExplosion always tags isExplosion=true), this is
// also what makes her base Chain Reaction passive's Instability marking fire reliably, instead of
// depending on an explosive weapon drop or perk roll (see DamageUtility.TryMarkExplodeOnDeath's own
// isExplosion gate).
component PixieExplosiveWeapon
{
    FP Radius;
    FP DamageMultiplier;

    // Probability (0-1) a shot's explosion actually fires. Replaces the earlier always-on behavior
    // (every single hit exploded), which the balance brief calls out as excessive - especially on a
    // high-Fire-Rate weapon, where it turned her sidearm into a continuous AoE stream and drowned out
    // her actual bomb identity.
    FP ProcChance;

    // Optional internal cooldown in seconds - 0 (the authored default) means off. Present purely so a
    // playtest can rein in a very high-Fire-Rate weapon from data if the per-shot chance alone turns
    // out not to be enough, rather than by hardcoding a limit in WeaponSystem.
    FP ProcCooldown;
}
